WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.849 --> 00:00:05.640
If you're looking for some screams to stream,
Netflix has quite a few good options stocked

00:00:05.640 --> 00:00:07.120
in its library right about now.

00:00:07.120 --> 00:00:11.440
In addition to some of the titles everyone
already knows about, like It Follows, The

00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:15.820
Babadook, The Conjuring and Hush, here are
some thrillers horror fans with a Netflix

00:00:15.820 --> 00:00:17.980
account won't want to miss.

00:00:17.980 --> 00:00:19.600
Last Shift

00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:24.410
Directed and co-written by Anthony DiBlasi,
this indie fright flick follows a rookie cop

00:00:24.410 --> 00:00:29.000
who's chosen to man an abandoned police station
the night before it closes for good.

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:34.359
The place is a cold, winding labyrinth, filled
with the eerie hum of fluorescent light bulbs.

00:00:34.359 --> 00:00:37.839
And from the moment our hero steps through
the door, weird things start happening in

00:00:37.839 --> 00:00:38.839
the hallways.

00:00:38.839 --> 00:00:43.620
There's a mysterious phone call from a frightened
girl, something is banging around in the back,

00:00:43.620 --> 00:00:46.300
and the furniture seems just a little too
frisky.

00:00:46.300 --> 00:00:50.800
Things keep getting weirder, especially when
the rookie learns the history of a Manson-style

00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:53.889
family and their weird connection to this
empty building.

00:00:53.889 --> 00:00:57.929
Soon, she's running from bloody spectres and
horrific visions.

00:00:57.929 --> 00:01:02.999
The horror never stops until the final bloody
showdown, so by the end of Last Shift, you'll

00:01:02.999 --> 00:01:06.520
be left mumbling incoherently right alongside
her.

00:01:06.520 --> 00:01:07.860
The Nightmare

00:01:07.860 --> 00:01:13.590
This 2015 documentary is about real-life terrors,
which makes it far scarier than any fictional

00:01:13.590 --> 00:01:14.590
horror story.

00:01:14.590 --> 00:01:19.729
The Nightmare examines the awful and upsetting
mystery of sleep paralysis, a condition that

00:01:19.729 --> 00:01:24.570
leaves its victims trapped in a conscious
dream as they see all sorts of horrible creatures

00:01:24.570 --> 00:01:25.630
around them.

00:01:25.630 --> 00:01:29.570
The film features eight people who suffer
from the disorder, and they describe in detail

00:01:29.570 --> 00:01:34.329
how they can hear the sounds of the underworld
each night, and how they're haunted by demonic

00:01:34.329 --> 00:01:35.420
shadow-men.

00:01:35.420 --> 00:01:40.859
If that weren't scary enough, their devilish
visions are also re-created on-camera, giving

00:01:40.859 --> 00:01:44.610
us a glimpse into the nightmare world these
people experience.

00:01:44.610 --> 00:01:48.900
Let's just say, you'll probably want to stock
up on caffeine to stave off your own slumber

00:01:48.900 --> 00:01:50.280
after this movie's over.

00:01:50.280 --> 00:01:52.670
I Am the Pretty Thing That Lives in the House

00:01:52.670 --> 00:01:57.329
A love letter to Gothic fiction, I am the
Pretty Thing that Lives in the House is an

00:01:57.329 --> 00:02:02.049
atmospheric horror movie that slowly crawls
past the camera like a Victorian dream.

00:02:02.049 --> 00:02:06.460
A narrator tells us in the opening minutes
that she'll be dead within the year.

00:02:06.460 --> 00:02:11.850
Her name is Lily, and she's a hospice nurse,
caring for an elderly novelist in an old house;

00:02:11.850 --> 00:02:16.440
one full of empty spaces and strange noises
which gets even creepier when Lily glimpses

00:02:16.440 --> 00:02:18.630
an eerily beautiful ghost.

00:02:18.630 --> 00:02:22.990
While you won't see any carnage, darkness
still permeates the film, from its ominous

00:02:22.990 --> 00:02:28.110
doorways and suspicious mold to a disturbing
little mystery novel about a truly terrible

00:02:28.110 --> 00:02:29.110
incident.

00:02:29.110 --> 00:02:34.180
Thanks to Ruth Wilson's sad and lonely performance
and a creeping sense of certain doom, this

00:02:34.180 --> 00:02:38.490
is one spooky gem that'll leave you unnerved
and more than a little worried about what

00:02:38.490 --> 00:02:40.960
might be standing right behind you.

00:02:40.960 --> 00:02:42.300
Under the Shadow

00:02:42.300 --> 00:02:46.590
There are plenty of evil spirits haunting
Under the Shadow, but this Iranian film knows

00:02:46.590 --> 00:02:51.680
there are scarier things than demons, like
the horrors of war or losing your kid.

00:02:51.680 --> 00:02:56.840
Set in Tehran during the Iran-Iraq War, the
film sheds light on citizens who sought shelter

00:02:56.840 --> 00:02:57.840
underground.

00:02:57.840 --> 00:03:02.810
That's the world our heroine finds herself
in, as she tries to protect her kid from bombs...

00:03:02.810 --> 00:03:04.750
and kidnapping djinn.

00:03:04.750 --> 00:03:09.020
These spirits are drawn to fear and anxiety,
looking for something to possess, but as a

00:03:09.020 --> 00:03:13.030
rational woman who doesn't believe in myths
or fairy tales, she has a hard time believing

00:03:13.030 --> 00:03:14.890
these creatures even exist…

00:03:14.890 --> 00:03:18.350
Until she starts seeing floating cloaks and
creepy old men.

00:03:18.350 --> 00:03:22.340
What result is some genuinely creepy moments
that'll stick with you.

00:03:22.340 --> 00:03:24.270
The Transfiguration

00:03:24.270 --> 00:03:28.870
Screen vampires tend to be either hideous
or completely seductive, but Milo from The

00:03:28.870 --> 00:03:32.170
Transfiguration stands apart from the fanged
crowd.

00:03:32.170 --> 00:03:36.770
This young orphan from New York's streets
lives an isolated life, running from bullies,

00:03:36.770 --> 00:03:42.200
visiting a counselor to discuss violent thoughts,
and watching disturbing animal videos online.

00:03:42.200 --> 00:03:45.280
But Milo is far more than your typical messed-up
kid.

00:03:45.280 --> 00:03:48.410
As he might put it himself, he's a "realistic"
vampire.

00:03:48.410 --> 00:03:52.410
This boy is obsessed with everything undead
and spends his spare time stabbing victims

00:03:52.410 --> 00:03:54.180
and drinking their blood.

00:03:54.180 --> 00:03:58.140
Despite his thirst for the red stuff, he's
not a supernatural being.

00:03:58.140 --> 00:04:00.880
He's just a mentally disturbed monster.

00:04:00.880 --> 00:04:05.120
Without a doubt, The Transfiguration is one
of the most disturbing vampire movies ever

00:04:05.120 --> 00:04:09.500
made and features a scene so horrific you
might have to stop watching.

00:04:09.500 --> 00:04:13.861
But despite the brutality, this flick is an
original take on a tired genre, so if you

00:04:13.861 --> 00:04:19.769
can stomach some serious gore, it might just
transfigure your opinion on vampires forever.

00:04:19.769 --> 00:04:20.920
The Ritual

00:04:20.920 --> 00:04:25.720
Forests are freaky places, and yet few films
utilize the environmental fright factor as

00:04:25.720 --> 00:04:27.040
well as The Ritual.

00:04:27.040 --> 00:04:31.110
The film follows four British city slickers,
hiking their way through Sweden, when they

00:04:31.110 --> 00:04:33.340
make the mistake of taking a shortcut.

00:04:33.340 --> 00:04:37.920
Their detour leads them into an incredibly
dense forest, where elk are impaled on trees

00:04:37.920 --> 00:04:40.580
and something big is moving in the woods.

00:04:40.580 --> 00:04:45.410
They encounter a creepy cabin, and are plagued
with nightmares that are a little too vivid.

00:04:45.410 --> 00:04:50.160
Meanwhile, the thing moving in the woods keeps
getting closer, just as our central hero's

00:04:50.160 --> 00:04:53.860
guilt over the violent loss of a friend starts
to take over.

00:04:53.860 --> 00:04:58.510
As the group encounters occult symbols and
pagan rituals, it becomes apparent this was

00:04:58.510 --> 00:05:02.440
the wrong place for a vacation, and we're
just as terrified as the characters when they

00:05:02.440 --> 00:05:04.800
stumble upon horror after horror.

00:05:04.800 --> 00:05:08.820
When they finally come face to face with the
thing that haunts them, it's one of the coolest-looking

00:05:08.820 --> 00:05:11.790
monster concepts in recent horror history.

00:05:11.790 --> 00:05:13.490
A Dark Song

00:05:13.490 --> 00:05:17.650
Far more than just your typical haunted house
movie, A Dark Song is a deep dive into the

00:05:17.650 --> 00:05:22.920
occult, a world of angels, demons, and complex
rituals that have to be performed in just

00:05:22.920 --> 00:05:24.960
the right way…or else.

00:05:24.960 --> 00:05:30.440
If magic were real, it would look like this:
methodical, miserable, and absolutely mad.

00:05:30.440 --> 00:05:35.120
The plot follows a grieving, determined woman
named Sophia who's prepared to spend months

00:05:35.120 --> 00:05:38.810
locked inside a house with an angry, overbearing
magician.

00:05:38.810 --> 00:05:43.320
In order to move on from her grief, she needs
to meet her guardian angel and ask it to grant

00:05:43.320 --> 00:05:44.590
her just one wish.

00:05:44.590 --> 00:05:49.060
But reaching out to the spirit world is a
lengthy process, and if she steps outside

00:05:49.060 --> 00:05:54.090
the house even once during the six month-long
ritual, she'll jeopardize her soul.

00:05:54.090 --> 00:05:59.500
The magic rituals are absolutely grueling,
and as tempers flare and time loses all meaning,

00:05:59.500 --> 00:06:04.669
the two characters begin falling apart, until
something from the other side peeks through.

00:06:04.669 --> 00:06:08.510
Needless to say, if you delve into black magic,
things are going to get dark, but if you're

00:06:08.510 --> 00:06:13.120
in the mood for a suspenseful slow burn and
a horror movie where the occult feels authentic

00:06:13.120 --> 00:06:17.260
and agonizing, then you should do your best
to summon A Dark Song on Netflix.

00:06:17.260 --> 00:06:18.600
Thanks for watching!

00:06:18.600 --> 00:06:21.400
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:06:21.400 --> 00:06:22.890
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

